    "summary": "Woman&#039;s wrapper (Anlo Ewe) made of imported industrial cotton, composed of twelve narrow strips machine-stitched together. The warp has a standard pattern of thin stripes of alternating blue and red cotton flanking a central broad orange stripe. The ground weft is of blue cotton, with variegated weft-faced blocks formed of twisted orange and yellow and white and yellow threads, with further double bands of plain weave in turquoise. Machine-hemmed at both warp ends.",
